\ port/gforth/host.4 - what relfsh needs of gforth beyond port/os.4,
\ loaded after port/kernel-io.4.

BASE @  DECIMAL

1 ARG-BASE !        \ argv: the engine, then the shell's own (--appl-image)
-1 ALLOCATE-ZEROES !  \ sys.fs's ALLOCATE is calloc

\ DICT-LIMIT is relf's address where the dictionary must stop, the stacks
\ being above it; the shell's only use is its guard for the forth
\ command's 16 KB gap (STACK-GAP-ROOM), which reports an overflow when the
\ gap would end within 8 KB of it. gforth's data stack is a region of its
\ own, STACK-CELLS deep (gforth's -d), so here it is that floor less those
\ 8 KB, from sp0 at boot.
VARIABLE DSTACK-TOP   0 DSTACK-TOP !
VARIABLE DSTACK-BYTES 0 DSTACK-BYTES !
: DSTACK-INIT ( --- )
  sp0 @ DSTACK-TOP !  STACK-CELLS CELLS DSTACK-BYTES ! ;   \ kernel.4's STACK-CELLS
: DICT-LIMIT ( --- a-addr )  DSTACK-TOP @ DSTACK-BYTES @ - 1024 +  8192 - ;

BASE !
